-- title:
--   Every element of λ-field over K is a quotient in the localised node ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, a field $k$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$, an element $l \in k$, and an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$. Let $x$ be a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying in `lambdaFieldOver q K`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(T)\!)$ generated by the constant series attached to the elements of $K$ together with the two series `lambdaModC` and `lambdaNModC _ q`. Write $R_0 =$ `lambdaLocalizedAtPoint q (coeffSubring A K) (redRestrict red K) l (l ^ q)` for the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(T)\!)$ consisting of those $f$ for which there exist two-variable polynomials $r, s$ with coefficients in the subring $A \cap K$ such that the evaluation of $s$ under $\mathrm{red}$ (restricted to $A \cap K$) at the point $(l, l^q)$ is nonzero and $f \cdot \mathrm{ev}(s) = \mathrm{ev}(r)$, where $\mathrm{ev}$ is evaluation of the two variables at `lambdaModC` and `lambdaNModC _ q` with coefficients sent to constant series. The conclusion asserts the existence of $y, z \in R_0$ with $z \neq 0$ and $x z = y$.
--
--   This is the inclusion of `lambdaFieldOver q K` into the set of fractions of elements of the localised level-two node ring $R_0$, i.e. one half of the statement that the former is the field of fractions of the latter; it is the `IsFractionRing`-type input for statements about $R_0$ and its normalisation inside that field. It is used by [`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.eq_of_isPrime_of_forall_lambdaEval_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.eq_of_isPrime_of_forall_lambdaEval_mem) and by [`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.isLocalization_atPrime_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_of_isIntegralElem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.isLocalization_atPrime_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_of_isIntegralElem).
